 "differences": [
  "Age, sex and handedness are left empty: the deposit's participants.tsv repeats the values of participants 1-10 for participants 11-20 and its summary (mean age 26.0, SD 3.9, range 21-34, 12 women) does not match the paper (30.25, SD 7.68, range 20-46, 11 women).",
  "Effective sampling rates of the physical-rotation head tracking are 74-90 Hz in many sessions, below the nominal 90 Hz (timestamps are as shared).",
  "The paper's Methods text for the ANOVA mentions eccentricities of 15, 30 and 45 deg while the Results use 45, 90 and 135 deg; not used here.",
  "The heading-error means in Fig. 1D and the ERSP epoch counts need the authors' preprocessing (heading error from yaw at the response, outlier removal, EEG) and were not reproduced."
 ],
